# Where move_char says no, and what flying, haste and slowness cost. In the Temple Square (3005): up is the air
# (3057). Flier (AfBy T) flies up and pays half; Sluggish (slow and sneaking, AfBy d and P) can't fly, pays double
# going east, leaves without a word, and sneak stops at once since the bit is already set. On the Levee (3049): south
# is the river (3203), which needs a boat; Rower carries a raft. Locksmith (a thief) tries the Mage's Bar (3018,
# south of 3017), and Melancholy's Room (3161), which is private once two are in it.
